---------------------------- MODULE 001_module ----------------------------
\* speclings tla 001: modules
\*
\* Welcome to the TLA+ track of speclings!
\*
\* This track is a collection of small, broken TLA+ specs. You learn to
\* read and write TLA+ by fixing them one at a time. Once you have fixed
\* one, save it and run speclings tla again to move on to the next. All
\* explanations are written as comments, like this one.
\*
\*   \* ...        comment to the end of the line
\*   (* ... *)     comment that may span several lines
\*
\* A TLA+ spec is written as a "module". A module starts with a header
\* like the first line of this file and ends with the ==== on the last
\* line.
\*
\*   ---- MODULE Name ----     any number of - (at least 4)
\*   ====                      any number of = (at least 4)
\*
\* Anything above the header or below the ==== is ignored.
\*
\* There is one rule: the module name must be the file name without .tla.
\* This file is named 001_module.tla.
\*
\* Now look at the first line.
=============================================================================
